# The chronicler's cost to the narration, measured: one fixed scripted run with the real model, played
# twice — with the chronicler and with --no-chronicler — and the [llm-timing] lines of the two log files
# compared by tools/journal/latency.py. Not part of the suite: it needs the model and takes minutes.
#
# The `wait for` holds are a player reading: they are what gives the chronicler the quiet it waits for,
# so the second visit's clicks land while it is writing the first visit up and have to preempt it.
#
# FLAGS: --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Hall" --period noon --observe-only "brewer" --cpu --no-llm-probe --llm-threads 4 --llm-seed 7

wait mode MainMenu 900
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 60
click continue
wait mode WorldView 600

# --- visit 1: the brewer ------------------------------------------------------------------
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 600
advance 20 900
wait for 6
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 20 900
wait for 6
click action 0
choose 0
advance 20 900
click continue
advance 20 900
wait for 6
state
click button
wait 600
advance 20 900
click button
wait mode WorldView 600

# --- the chronicler takes visit 1 up while the player reads the map ------------------------
wait for 10

# --- visit 2: every click below may land on a chronicler job and has to preempt it --------
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 600
advance 20 900
wait for 6
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 20 900
wait for 6
click action 0
choose 0
advance 20 900
click continue
advance 20 900
wait for 8
click button
wait 600
advance 20 900
click button
wait mode WorldView 600
wait for 240
inspect journal
crash-report latency
quit
